Belgium", "slug": "belgium"}], "biography": "Raoul Servais (1 May 1928 – 17 March 2023) was a Belgian filmmaker, animator and comics artist. He was born in Ostend, Belgium, and is a fundamental figure of the Belgian animation scene, as well as the founder of the animation faculty of the Royal Academy of Fine Arts (KASK).Servais was best known for the animated film, Harpya, for which he won a Palme d'Or at the 1979 Cannes Film Festival. Servais received the Lifetime Achievement Award at the World Festival of Animated Film - Animafest Zagreb in 2016. At the 9th Magritte Awards, he received an Honorary Magritte Award from the Académie André Delvaux.\nIn total, Servais won about 60 film prizes. Homages with retrospectives were organized in Paris, Madrid, Istanbul, Montreal, New York, Tokyo, Hong Kong, Rio de Janeiro and St Petersburg.Servais died at his home in Leffinge on 17 March 2023, at the age of 94.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T16:42:02.950175+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 4950, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raoul_Servais"}], "uuid": "b19acbe9-0201-4b0a-9629-6afa0a366471", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "27126", "external_references": [{"id": 25566, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q1394440"}, {"id": 30981, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "95662219"}, {"id": 30982, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n81008073"}, {"id": 30983, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n81008073"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-13T12:32:07.119216+10:00"}, {"id": 13826, "name": "Karel Zeman", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 859397, "title": "The Temptation of Mr Prokouk", "work_id": 73607, "role": "director", "role_id": 938, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 849505, "title": "A Christmas dream [English version]", "work_id": 66098, "role": "director", "role_id": 938, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 878240, "title": "Mr Prokouk becomes an inventor", "work_id": 91165, "role": "director", "role_id": 938, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1910-11-03", "date_of_death": "1989-04-05", "genders": [{"id": 9, "name": "Male", "slug": "male"}], "languages": [{"id": 20, "name": "Czech", "slug": "czech"}, {"id": 4, "name": "French", "slug": "french"}], "places_of_operation": [{"id": 55, "name": "Czechoslovakia", "slug": "czechoslovakia"}], "biography": "Karel Zeman (3 November 1910 – 5 April 1989) was a Czech film director, artist, production designer and animator, best known for directing fantasy films combining live-action footage with animation. Because of his creative use of special effects and animation in his films, he has often been called the \"Czech Méliès\".", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T15:46:21+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 4463, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karel_Zeman"}], "uuid": "0407529f-eb77-4d41-878d-5b53401d2456", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "22984", "external_references": [{"id": 24987, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q282000"}, {"id": 29724, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "70477444"}, {"id": 29725, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "n88092981"}, {"id": 29726, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-n88092981"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-13T14:55:41.095727+10:00"}, {"id": 13822, "name": "Opera Australia", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2198437, "title": "Don Giovanni", "work_id": 83732, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2190544, "title": "Die Fledermaus", "work_id": 83082, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2178462, "title": "Orphee et Eurydice", "work_id": 84198, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 794124, "title": "Hansel and Gretel by Engelbert Humperdinck", "work_id": 86809, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 782007, "title": "Lucia di Lammermoor", "work_id": 83326, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 906083, "title": "Nabucco", "work_id": 86812, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 898967, "title": "The Mikado", "work_id": 79458, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 801464, "title": "Encore! : the best of Joan Sutherland", "work_id": 89009, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 867493, "title": "The Merry widow", "work_id": 83322, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 738428, "title": "Chorus and principals on stage please: the making of Lakme", "work_id": 66094, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2081988, "title": "Adriana Lecouvreur", "work_id": 83578, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "Opera Australia is the principal opera company in Australia. Based in Sydney, its performance season at the Sydney Opera House accompanied by the Opera Australia Orchestra runs for approximately eight months of the year, with the remainder of its time spent at the Arts Centre Melbourne, where it is accompanied by Orchestra Victoria. In 2004, the company gave 226 performances in its subscription seasons in Sydney and Melbourne, attended by more than 294,000 people.It is funded by government grants, corporate sponsorship, private philanthropy, and ticket sales. The proportion of its revenue from ticket sales is considerably higher than that of most companies, approximately 75 per cent. The company is perhaps best known internationally for its association with Dame Joan Sutherland, for Baz Luhrmann's production of Puccini's La bohème in the early 1990s and more recently, for, apart from performances inside the opera house, large scale outdoor performances on Sydney Harbour.\nMany thousands of Australians also experience the company's work through television, radio, video, compact disc, DVD, and the annual free performance of opera in the Domain in Sydney. The company also performs in an annual outdoor event at Mrs Macquarie's Chair, Handa Opera on Sydney Harbour, where since 2012 operas such as La traviata, Madama Butterfly, Turandot, Aida and Carmen have played.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-09-05T23:37:21.892111+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 6075, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opera_Australia"}], "uuid": "6abb559d-7fc3-4dbc-9610-a3b359cdc198", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "4745", "external_references": [{"id": 42593, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q2916790"}, {"id": 55399, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "131870182"}, {"id": 55400, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "no2003022479"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-05T23:37:24.659673+10:00"}, {"id": 13821, "name": "OTC Australia", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 889185, "title": "OTC memories", "work_id": 99031, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2066694, "title": "A Chord for voices", "work_id": 66092, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": "2023-05-09T11:24:15.671096+10:00", "external_links": [], "uuid": "de71723b-fd00-4b03-bd3d-3b09926913fb", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug"